{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>All his sons.</b> These are the tribes. <b>And all his daughters.</b> This is Dinah and Serach bat Asher. <b>And he refused to be comforted.</b> Because a person cannot accept consolation for one who is alive yet believed to be dead — for concerning the dead it was decreed that he be forgotten from the heart, but not concerning the living. <b>For I will go down to my son mourning into Sheol.</b> That is to say, in mourning I will be buried, and I will not be comforted all the days of my life." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> Sheol — Gehinnom. For he was confident that not one of them would die in his lifetime, and when Yosef was lost in his lifetime, he feared for himself the punishment of Gehinnom, for this testified to his wickedness: had his merit been complete, not one of his sons would die in his lifetime." "<b>And his father wept for him.</b> This is Yitzhak, who was weeping on account of the trouble of Yaakov his son, but he was not mourning, for he knew that Yosef was alive."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:29.055045333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}